    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30501" root="عمد" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُمُدَّانٌ</span></b>  (O, K, TA, in the CK <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُمَّدان</span>) <i>Tall;</i>
(O, K;) applied to a man; fem. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>, applied
to a woman: (O:) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعْمَدٌ</span></b> , (A, K,) like
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُكْرَمٌ</span> [in measure], (K,) or ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعَمَّدٌ</span></b> , (O,) signifies the same, (A, O, K,) applied to a man; (A;)
and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَوِيلُ العِمَادِ</span></b> . (Mbr, L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُمُدٌّ</span>, in two places.

